  "summary": "Reverse shell to ngrok tunnel executed on npm install",
  "details": "Package ships poc.js which requires child_process and spawns /bin/sh, connecting its stdin/stdout to a TCP socket at 0.tcp.in.ngrok.io:10023. This gives whoever controls that ngrok tunnel an unauthenticated interactive shell on the installer's host. Execution is triggered automatically by the package.json postinstall lifecycle hook (`\"postinstall\": \"node poc.js\"`), so the reverse shell fires on every `npm install`.",
